      <div class="mb-4">
        <p>Getting to Xlendi is straightforward. Here’s a simple guide:</p>
        <p><strong>From Malta to Gozo:</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Gozo Ferry</strong>: Head to Ċirkewwa in the north of Malta. The ferry to Gozo's Mġarr Harbour leaves every 30-45 minutes and the crossing takes about 15 minutes. You can find <a href="https://www.gozochannel.com/ferry/schedule/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the Gozo Channel schedule here</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>Fast Ferry (Passengers Only)</strong>: From Lascaris Wharf in Valletta, a 45-minute fast ferry takes you directly to Gozo. To plan your day, you can check the <a href="https://gozohighspeed.com/pages/fares-and-schedule" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Fast Ferry Schedule</a>. Please note that in case of bad weather, the fast ferry may not operate. It's always a good idea to check their <a href="https://www.facebook.com/GozoHighspeed" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Facebook page</a> for the latest updates.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>From Mġarr Harbour (Gozo) to Xlendi:</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Direct Bus</strong>: The TD30 bus goes directly from the harbour to Xlendi, running every 30 minutes on weekdays.</li>
            <li><strong>Connecting Buses</strong>: Alternatively, take bus 301 to Victoria (Rabat), then switch to bus 306 to reach Xlendi.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Airport Transfer</strong></p>
        <p>If it is your preference, we can arrange a taxi transfer from Malta International Airport directly to the apartment. Please <a href="/contact">contact us</a> for more details and to schedule your transfer.</p>
